{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>In Shushan the capital the Jews killed.</b> They are the men of Mordecai; they are the Jews who were in Shushan, who killed their enemies in Shushan. Therefore Scripture says, \"To the Jews who were in Shushan,\" and \"the decree was also given in Shushan,\" and \"the Jews who were in Shushan gathered\" — and it did not mention \"the capital.\" The meaning of \"they gathered\" is that they had been scattered in the streets."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:20.740285387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}